From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 20:40:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/15] native: repaint a display as soon as it stops scanning
 out a window

When a fullscreen window stops qualifying for direct scanout, nothing in
the stage necessarily asks for a repaint: a window that leaves fullscreen
is frozen by the shell while it waits for the client to resize, and
damage from a frozen window queues no redraw. The display kept showing
the last client buffer until something else redrew the stage.

Check every dispatched frame of a view that is scanning out whether its
window still qualifies, and repaint the whole view when it doesn't. Size
changes and disabling unredirection schedule a frame so the check runs
even when no client commits. The first composited frame after scanout
covers the whole view, since the plane showed a client buffer before it
and partial damage would be relative to an older frame of our own.

With com.lantharos.kestrel.diagnostics log-direct-scanout enabled, the
compositor logs when a display starts and stops scanning out a window,
why it stopped, and how long the desktop took to come back.
